usage: zgate COMMAND [--repo DIR] [--jobs N] ...
  snap TAG                 keep bin/zc, bin/zl and HEAD's tree as snapshot TAG
  cdiff REF NEW OUT [--set corpus|wide] [--normalise] [--ref-system DIR]
                           the C (and dumps) of every program, REF's against NEW's
  ab OLDZC NEWZC OLDTREE [NEWTREE]
                           the allocation split of a self-compile
  asan ZC FILE [ARGS]      build FILE with ASan and UBSan, and run it
  pregate                  the quick checks of the .z files changed since HEAD
  run TAG OUT [SHA]        the per-batch gate of SHA (HEAD) against snapshot TAG
  time ci|gates OUT [SHA]  make ci, or each ci-gates leg alone, timed
The repository is the current directory, or --repo DIR; snapshots and the run
lock live in $ZGATE_HOME (default ~/.cache/zerolang/gate).
